# Search

State what a site search covers before the first query. Documentation search covers documentation, so results must say what type of page they are and must never be read as a search of household data. Home Assistant’s own search keeps finding entities and actions. Scope, result count, empty states, focus and the no-JavaScript fallback follow the [shared finder behaviour](../finder.html#finder-shared-contract).

## When to use it

Use a local site search that may span guidance, components and examples, provided it states its scope.

## Home Assistant boundary

Do not blend public documentation with private entity records. Do not send household queries to an external index without an explicit product decision. Results link to existing pages and identify their type.

